      ":question/id": "890bb78e-a28f-5687-b16c-3c101e5dfb94",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-8y &=5 \\\\ x-2y &=1 \\\\ x-3y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 2\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent independent.",
