      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+3y &=3 \\\\ -x+y &=5 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{5}{2}y &=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, select: The system is consistent independent.",
